{"at": "2026-11-03T13:27:49Z", "commit_ref": "57d73ea", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Section planner: wrote specs/0050/.spec-md (steering narrative) and specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl (47 sections) implementing specs/0050/.manual/001 in its §S order.\n\nPlan shape:\n- S1 is split into 7 parts: axis data, mandatory complexity, preset GUIDs, entry files, catalogue export, CatalogueImport, seed deletion.\n- S2 into 4, S3 into 3, S4 into 4, S5 into 3; S6 is one part.\n- S7 into 2, S8 into 4, S9 into 4, S10 into 3, S11 into 5, S12 into 2, S13 into 2, S14 into 2.\n- A Close part carries the final WIRE_UI and the whole-suite gates.\n\nInvariants:\n- Every section carries elev-list-empty, no-vstest and no-kit-kit-json.\n- 001 §T's greps and the removal greps (EpsAxisEvaluated, optional complexity, seeded preset string ids, the Seeding seam, Test DB / MSSQL keys, VersionsInUse, the Scene / ExperimentCollection seams, recent.json, measuredElementOf, the archive Mueller proxy, SolverHandoff) are declared on every section AFTER the one that establishes them. Ids are prefixed per section.\n\nInterpretations recorded in .spec-md §3:\n- Both closure routes become axis data: tabulated, and the transcendental EpsAxisEvaluated case.\n- complexity becomes mandatory.\n- Presets get frozen GUIDs, while the well-known id modules stay.\n- The Seeding project moves into Domain as CatalogueImport.\n- Storage.fsproj ships Catalogue/Builtin.\n- Start-up import auto-applies only the rows that overwrite nothing.\n- Registered catalogue folders are import-log rows.\n- A KitFolderPicker seam lets S4 open kits before S5's start screen exists.\n- A read-only open writes nothing.\n- AT-1 builds its kit around a copy of the lab folder.\n- Item models reference the existing presets and samples.\n- The crystal builders (buildTriclinic, buildAbsorbing) are promoted into MuellerInverse.fs rather than moved to BerremanTestSupport. This deviates from 001 §Q's list, because product materials need them.\n- The noise-model data types move to Domain in S7.1, and the functions to Optimization in S10.1.\n- The MSSQL keys are dropped.\n- AGF import is in scope; Materials Project, paywalled and gyration adapters are out.\n- data.zip's shapes JSONs are kept under data/reference/shapes.\n"}
